# The lock screen runs its PAM conversation as the session user, while Howdy
# keeps its models and scripts readable by root only, so the face helper behind
# the omarchy-lock-face line re-executes its packaged copy through this rule.
# No arguments: the account to match comes from SUDO_USER, which sudo itself
# sets after env_reset, so a user can only ever match their own face, and the
# outcome is a verdict for PAM, never a session or a file.
%wheel ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/omarchy-face-match ""
